OL,3,GWales                                  
OL,5,CToday:FThere will be the odd bright    
OL,6,Fspell near western coasts at first,    
OL,7,Fbut cloudy across Wales for much of    
OL,8,FThursday. It will feel cold with a     
OL,9,Fgentle easterly breeze and             
OL,10,Ftemperatures below average.            
OL,12,CTonight:FIt will turn wet and breezier 
OL,13,Ftonight rain arrives and sweeps across 
OL,14,FWales through the morning.             
OL,15,FTemperatures recover in the west, but  
OL,16,Fstill chilly inland with patchy frost. 
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
